{
  "class": "java.lang.Integer",
  "_note": [
    "Fourth bb-allowlist parity battery. Integer extension covers the",
    "bit-twiddle family (bitCount, numberOfLeadingZeros, etc.) +",
    "compare/signum/hashCode/sum. Constants (MIN_VALUE/MAX_VALUE/SIZE/",
    "BYTES) are static fields; case battery doesn't test those — they",
    "carry through the AOT path's getstatic lowering, not method",
    "dispatch. Java's int is 32-bit; PHP int is 64-bit. Caller bytecode",
    "narrows at storage points; the case spec passes values within",
    "[Integer.MIN_VALUE, Integer.MAX_VALUE] so the contract holds.",
    "",
    "JSON ints decode as Long; reflection picks the (long)... overload",
    "where Java has both int and long. Integer methods take int — most",
    "have no long overload, so reflection auto-narrows the Long arg",
    "to int. Values outside int range would fail the reflection check;",
    "the cases below stay in range."
  ],
